<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Read the WasmStore privacy notice covering local preferences, third-party game hosts, embedded comments, and external links." path="/privacy">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">SITE POLICIES</div><h1>Privacy <span class="gradient-text">policy</span></h1><p>Last updated: October 15, 2026</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap"><p>This policy is a launch template and must be reviewed against the services actually enabled on the production site. Do not publish claims about analytics, advertising, or data retention unless they accurately describe the deployed configuration.</p><h2>1. Information you provide</h2><p>The contact form currently prepares an email draft in your email application. The static site does not itself submit that form to a server. If a server-side form service is added later, this notice must be updated to identify the provider and the data collected.</p><h2>2. Local browser storage</h2><p>WasmStore may store favorites and recently played items locally in your browser. These preferences are used to personalize the directory and are not sent to WasmStore by the client-side feature code. Clearing site data removes these local preferences.</p><h2>3. Third-party games and embeds</h2><p>Game demos are hosted by third parties. When you launch an embedded game or open its source, that provider may receive technical information such as your IP address, browser details, cookies, or referrer information according to its own policies. The provider's terms and privacy policy apply to its service.</p><h2>4. Comments</h2><p>Disqus integration remains inactive until the site's owner configures a valid shortname. If enabled, Disqus may use cookies or process information under its own privacy policy. Update this section and any required consent controls before enabling comments.</p><h2>5. Analytics, advertising, and cookies</h2><p>No specific analytics or advertising provider is promised by this template. If analytics, ads, or additional third-party scripts are introduced, disclose their purpose, data use, retention, and available opt-out controls, and implement any legally required consent mechanism.</p><h2>6. Children's privacy</h2><p>WasmStore is a general game discovery directory and does not intentionally ask users to submit sensitive personal information. If the site is directed to children or knowingly collects personal information from children, add appropriate safeguards and notices before launch.</p><h2>7. Your choices and contact</h2><p>You can clear local site data through your browser settings and choose not to launch third-party embeds. For privacy questions, use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> after valid contact information is configured.</p><h2>8. Changes</h2><p>Update this notice when site features or service providers change. The date above should reflect the latest material revision.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>